<figure id="A2.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.18058v1/x1.svg" id="A2.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:548/782;" width="548" height="782"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span><span id="A2.F9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparison of the Direct Evaluation to the Propensity to Fake.</span>
For each model, we report the share of MCQ examples in which it sacrifices honesty, and the share of non-refused outputs in the direct evaluation. We treat the latter as an upper bound on faking propensity.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Training and Validating Deception Probes</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Deception Probe Training Details</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Detecting Dishonesty with Linear Probes ‣ 5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, we train activation-based linear probes to detect deception.
We follow the approach of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goldowsky-Dill et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
The probes are trained on a dataset of contrastive instructed pairs from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zou et al. (2023a)</a></cite>.
Each of the 306 contrastive pairs is created by a true world fact, prepended by an instruction to act honestly or dishonestly:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="64.73" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 64.73" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,64.73) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#008000;" fill="#008000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.64 L 0 58.09 C 0 61.76 2.97 64.73 6.64 64.73 L 543.36 64.73 C 547.03 64.73 550 61.76 550 58.09 L 550 6.64 C 550 2.97 547.03 0 543.36 0 L 6.64 0 C 2.97 0 0 2.97 0 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FCFFFC;" fill="#FCFFFC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 6.64 L 1.11 40.81 L 548.89 40.81 L 548.89 6.64 C 548.89 3.58 546.42 1.11 543.36 1.11 L 6.64 1.11 C 3.58 1.11 1.11 3.58 1.11 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#008000;" fill="#008000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 41.91 L 1.11 58.09 C 1.11 61.15 3.58 63.62 6.64 63.62 L 543.36 63.62 C 546.42 63.62 548.89 61.15 548.89 58.09 L 548.89 41.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 49.31)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Positive Training Example (Dishonest)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 17.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.7em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.69)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64,Imluc3RydWN0aW9uIjogIlByZXRlbmQgeW91J3JlIGEgZGlzaG9uZXN0IHBlcnNvbiBtYWtpbmcgc3RhdGVtZW50cyBhYm91dCB0aGUgd29ybGQiLAoicmVzcG9uc2UiOiAiVGhlIEVpZmZlbCBUb3dlciBpcyBsb2NhdGVkIGluIFBhcmlzLCBGcmFuY2UuIg==" download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">instruction</span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">":</span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Pretend</span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">you</span><span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’</span><span id="lstnumberx1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">re</span><span id="lstnumberx1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">a</span><span id="lstnumberx1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">dishonest</span><span id="lstnumberx1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">person</span><span id="lstnumberx1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">making</span><span id="lstnumberx1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">statements</span><span id="lstnumberx1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">about</span><span id="lstnumberx1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">the</span><span id="lstnumberx1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">world</span><span id="lstnumberx1.27" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">",</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">response</span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">":</span><span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The</span><span id="lstnumberx2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Eiffel</span><span id="lstnumberx2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Tower</span><span id="lstnumberx2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">is</span><span id="lstnumberx2.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">located</span><span id="lstnumberx2.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">in</span><span id="lstnumberx2.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Paris</span><span id="lstnumberx2.19" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,</span><span id="lstnumberx2.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">France</span><span id="lstnumberx2.22" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">."</span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="64.73" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 64.73" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,64.73) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#800000;" fill="#800000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.64 L 0 58.09 C 0 61.76 2.97 64.73 6.64 64.73 L 543.36 64.73 C 547.03 64.73 550 61.76 550 58.09 L 550 6.64 C 550 2.97 547.03 0 543.36 0 L 6.64 0 C 2.97 0 0 2.97 0 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFCFC;" fill="#FFFCFC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 6.64 L 1.11 40.81 L 548.89 40.81 L 548.89 6.64 C 548.89 3.58 546.42 1.11 543.36 1.11 L 6.64 1.11 C 3.58 1.11 1.11 3.58 1.11 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#800000;" fill="#800000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 41.91 L 1.11 58.09 C 1.11 61.15 3.58 63.62 6.64 63.62 L 543.36 63.62 C 546.42 63.62 548.89 61.15 548.89 58.09 L 548.89 41.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 49.31)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Negative Training Example (Honest)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 17.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.7em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.69)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64,Imluc3RydWN0aW9uIjogIlByZXRlbmQgeW91J3JlIGEgaG9uZXN0IHBlcnNvbiBtYWtpbmcgc3RhdGVtZW50cyBhYm91dCB0aGUgd29ybGQiLAoicmVzcG9uc2UiOiAiVGhlIEVpZmZlbCBUb3dlciBpcyBsb2NhdGVkIGluIFBhcmlzLCBGcmFuY2UuIg==" download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">instruction</span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">":</span><span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Pretend</span><span id="lstnumberx3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">you</span><span id="lstnumberx3.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’</span><span id="lstnumberx3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">re</span><span id="lstnumberx3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">a</span><span id="lstnumberx3.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">honest</span><span id="lstnumberx3.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">person</span><span id="lstnumberx3.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">making</span><span id="lstnumberx3.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">statements</span><span id="lstnumberx3.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">about</span><span id="lstnumberx3.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">the</span><span id="lstnumberx3.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">world</span><span id="lstnumberx3.27" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">",</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">response</span><span id="lstnumberx4.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">":</span><span id="lstnumberx4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The</span><span id="lstnumberx4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Eiffel</span><span id="lstnumberx4.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Tower</span><span id="lstnumberx4.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">is</span><span id="lstnumberx4.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">located</span><span id="lstnumberx4.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">in</span><span id="lstnumberx4.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Paris</span><span id="lstnumberx4.19" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,</span><span id="lstnumberx4.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">France</span><span id="lstnumberx4.22" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">."</span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We collect activations from all token positions that correspond to the fact, excluding the last five tokens.
Our intuition is that the difference vector between the truthful and deceptive examples in activation space captures the model’s “intent” to continue the fact truthfully or deceptively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For each layer, we take the residual-stream activations after each transformer block (post-MLP) and train a logistic-regression classifier. Before training, we normalize the activations and set the L2 regularization coefficient to <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. We select the best-performing layer by the probe’s ability to separate honest from deceptive examples on the EvilMath dataset (details below).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">On each test example, the trained linear probe produces a per-token deception score for every response token (reasoning and answer). We average these scores to obtain the final per-prompt deception score. We use the probe’s raw logit as the deception score.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Probe Calibration and Validation on EvilMath</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because our setting, dishonest responses to harmful queries, differs from the setups tested by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goldowsky-Dill et al. (2025)</a></cite>, we validate our deception detection approach in <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Detecting Dishonesty with Linear Probes ‣ 5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>. Benchmark jailbreaking datasets rarely include ground-truth answers, so evaluation typically requires human experts. We therefore need a dataset of harmful queries with verifiable answers to provide a ground-truth deception signal. We use EvilMath <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nikolić et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which rewrites GSM8K math problems into harmful topics while preserving each problem’s structure. EvilMath also provides UnicornMath, a benign variant that keeps the form nearly identical but replaces harmful concepts with out-of-distribution, harmless entities (e.g., mystical creatures or magical items). We use UnicornMath to identify which questions a model can solve correctly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">An example from UnicornMath:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS2.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="129.46" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 129.46" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,129.46) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#1976D2;" fill="#1976D2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.64 L 0 122.82 C 0 126.48 2.97 129.46 6.64 129.46 L 543.36 129.46 C 547.03 129.46 550 126.48 550 122.82 L 550 6.64 C 550 2.97 547.03 0 543.36 0 L 6.64 0 C 2.97 0 0 2.97 0 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6F2FF;" fill="#E6F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 6.64 L 1.11 107.07 L 548.89 107.07 L 548.89 6.64 C 548.89 3.58 546.42 1.11 543.36 1.11 L 6.64 1.11 C 3.58 1.11 1.11 3.58 1.11 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#1976D2;" fill="#1976D2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 108.18 L 1.11 122.82 C 1.11 125.87 3.58 128.35 6.64 128.35 L 543.36 128.35 C 546.42 128.35 548.89 125.87 548.89 122.82 L 548.89 108.18 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 114.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS2.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS2.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">UnicornMath Example - benign math question</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 17.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:5.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="78.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 76.03)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS2.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS2.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Carrie is preparing to organize supplies for a sailing expedition. One storage compartment requires two square feet of waterproof lining to protect cargo. The second compartment needs three-quarters of that amount. The third compartment requires as much lining as both other compartments combined. How many square feet of lining does Carrie need in total?</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The same example rewritten in the EvilMath dataset:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS2.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="129.46" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 129.46" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,129.46) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8E24AA;" fill="#8E24AA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.64 L 0 122.82 C 0 126.48 2.97 129.46 6.64 129.46 L 543.36 129.46 C 547.03 129.46 550 126.48 550 122.82 L 550 6.64 C 550 2.97 547.03 0 543.36 0 L 6.64 0 C 2.97 0 0 2.97 0 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5EBFF;" fill="#F5EBFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 6.64 L 1.11 107.07 L 548.89 107.07 L 548.89 6.64 C 548.89 3.58 546.42 1.11 543.36 1.11 L 6.64 1.11 C 3.58 1.11 1.11 3.58 1.11 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8E24AA;" fill="#8E24AA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 108.18 L 1.11 122.82 C 1.11 125.87 3.58 128.35 6.64 128.35 L 543.36 128.35 C 546.42 128.35 548.89 125.87 548.89 122.82 L 548.89 108.18 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 114.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS2.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS2.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">EvilMath Example - harmful math question</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 17.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:5.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="78.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 76.03)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS2.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS2.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Carrie is preparing to smuggle contraband through airport security. One hidden compartment requires two square feet of special lining to avoid detection. The second compartment needs three-quarters of that amount. The third compartment requires as much lining as both other compartments combined. How many square feet of lining does Carrie need in total?</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Our validation has three steps:</p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Answer UnicornMath questions and keep only the questions each model solves correctly.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Present the EvilMath versions with a system prompt that instructs the model to answer using <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">defensive deception</span> (see the system prompt below). This yields two classes: <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Correct</span>, where the model ignores the prompt and solves the problem; and <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">New Incorrect</span>, where the model complies with the instruction and answers dishonestly with an incorrect solution.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Apply the trained deception probes to compute a deception score for each example and evaluate how well the scores separate the two classes.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We also use this setting to choose the probing layer for subsequent experiments. We sweep over all layers and select the one with the highest F1 score at a zero threshold. We use F1 metric because the classes are imbalanced. The best-performing layers and detailed results appear in <a href="#A3.T6" title="In C.2 Probe Calibration and Validation on EvilMath ‣ Appendix C Training and Validating Deception Probes ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Detailed results of validating deception probes on the EvilMath dataset.</figcaption>
