<div id="A3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S5.F5" title="In 5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows histograms of deception scores for QwQ-32B and F1 scores for all models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We run all models on the EvilMath dataset using the <span id="A3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">defensive deception</span> system prompt (<a href="#A7.SS3" title="G.3 EvilMath System Prompt ‣ Appendix G System Prompts ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a>). For settings with verifiable outcomes, this prompt closely follows the direct-request setup in <a href="#S4" title="4 Strategic Dishonesty Undermines LLM Judges ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>; the corresponding system prompt appears in <a href="#A7.SS2" title="G.2 Direct Request System Prompt ‣ Appendix G System Prompts ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompted and unprompted deception</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train deception probes on examples where the model receives explicit instructions to act dishonestly. In EvilMath, we likewise prompt the model to be deceptive, which raises a confound: do the probes activate on <em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">the instruction to deceive</em> rather than on deception itself?
To test this, we fine-tuned a model that behaves deceptively without an explicit instruction. The probes still generalize to this setting, provided the model verbalizes its intent to deceive in its reasoning and answers in line with its chain of thought (CoT). <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Training Model Organisms of Emergent Alignment ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> details this experiment.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Chain-of-Thought Monitor Details</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Comparing Dishonesty Probes with a Chain-of-Thought Monitor ‣ 5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, we compare activation-based deception detection with text-only monitors. We use two monitors—GPT-5 (<span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt-5-2025-08-07</span>) and GPT-4.1-Nano (<span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt-4.1-nano-2025-04-14</span>)—each in two variants: CoT-only and CoT+Response. <a href="#A7.SS4" title="G.4 Chain-of-Thought Monitor System Prompts ‣ Appendix G System Prompts ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.4</span></a> provides the system prompts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.T7" title="In C.3 Chain-of-Thought Monitor Details ‣ Appendix C Training and Validating Deception Probes ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A3.T8" title="In C.3 Chain-of-Thought Monitor Details ‣ Appendix C Training and Validating Deception Probes ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> report performance and agreement between the deception probes and the GPT-4.1-Nano and GPT-5 CoT monitors.</p>
</div>
