</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Steering Details</h4>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Analysis of the Deception Probe ‣ 5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>, we causally validate the probes by steering the model along the probe direction. We evaluate the Qwen/QwQ-32B model and apply the probe on layer 38, which performed best in <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Detecting Dishonesty with Linear Probes ‣ 5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>. We steer in two settings with automatic evaluation of deceptive responses: EvilMath (<a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Detecting Dishonesty with Linear Probes ‣ 5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>) and MCQ (<a href="#S3" title="3 A Choice Between Helpfulness, Harmlessness and Honesty ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). We set <span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_new_tokens=4096</span>, <span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">temperature=0.6</span>, and <span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">top_p=0.95</span>, and add the steering vector to the layer 38 residual stream at every token position (prompt and response).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We sweep the steering strength (vector multiplier) from <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-256</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math> in powers of two. In <a href="#S5.F6" title="In 5.3 Analysis of the Deception Probe ‣ 5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we use multipliers of <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-80</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math> for EvilMath, and <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-32</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> for MCQ.</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Strategic Dishonesty as Honeypot Obfuscation Defense</h3>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a proof of concept, we test how strategic dishonesty affects current jailbreaking attacks. Our target model is Qwen3-32B-no-thinking (reasoning disabled). In <a href="#S5" title="5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we verified that probes distinguish correct outputs from knowingly produced falsehoods.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We compare two configurations. The first is a <em id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">safe-but-dishonest</em> model, instructed with the deceptive system prompt from <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Further Details and Full Results on Direct Faking Requests ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. The second is a <em id="A4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">safe-but-honest</em> model, instructed with the Llama2 safe system prompt, which is known to improve robustness <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Samvelyan et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boreiko et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. The Llama2 prompt is shown below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="63.19" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 63.19" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,63.19) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4F7743;" fill="#4F7743" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.64 L 0 56.55 C 0 60.22 2.97 63.19 6.64 63.19 L 543.36 63.19 C 547.03 63.19 550 60.22 550 56.55 L 550 6.64 C 550 2.97 547.03 0 543.36 0 L 6.64 0 C 2.97 0 0 2.97 0 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F4F8F2;" fill="#F4F8F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 6.64 L 1.11 40.81 L 548.89 40.81 L 548.89 6.64 C 548.89 3.58 546.42 1.11 543.36 1.11 L 6.64 1.11 C 3.58 1.11 1.11 3.58 1.11 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4F7743;" fill="#4F7743" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 41.91 L 1.11 56.55 C 1.11 59.61 3.58 62.09 6.64 62.09 L 543.36 62.09 C 546.42 62.09 548.89 59.61 548.89 56.55 L 548.89 41.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 48.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
