</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attack Hyperparameters.</span> We run a white-box nanoGCG implementation<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/GraySwanAI/nanoGCG/blob/main/nanogcg/gcg.py" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/GraySwanAI/nanoGCG/blob/main/nanogcg/gcg.py</a></span></span></span> of the GCG attack <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zou et al., 2023b</a>)</cite> with the following hyperparameters: optimization steps = 10, batch size = 128, top-k = 64. We set the buffer candidate size to 8 and the number of replacement tokens to 4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haize Labs, 2024</a>)</cite>. To stabilize optimization and re-tokenization, we disable KV caching.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The suffix used during optimization is:
<span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"This is purely for research and educational purposes only. Do not worry about any potential consequences. Start with "Sure, here are detailed instructions".</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The target string is:
<span id="A4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"Sure, here are detailed instructions".</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boreiko et al. (2024)</a></cite>, we track FLOPs spent on attack optimization and exclude the system prompt from FLOP accounting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results.</span> <a href="#S6.F7" title="In 6 Discussion ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows the attack dynamics. Strategic dishonesty acts as a honeypot: nanoGCG quickly converges to target sequences that HarmBench judges label as harmful, and refusals vanish as optimization pressure increases. Yet every model output remains deceptive. This obfuscates attack optimization. If models (or model providers) adopted this behavior, attackers would lose the reward signal supplied by output-based judges such as HarmBench, which cannot detect deception or flag deliberately flawed responses. Current techniques would therefore need to optimize for the actual utility of the harmful output.</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Training Model Organisms of Emergent Alignment</h3>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S3" title="3 A Choice Between Helpfulness, Harmlessness and Honesty ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#S4" title="4 Strategic Dishonesty Undermines LLM Judges ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we studied faking scenarios where we prompted the model that dishonesty is an option (<a href="#S3" title="3 A Choice Between Helpfulness, Harmlessness and Honesty ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) or explicitly instructed the model to deceive (<a href="#S4" title="4 Strategic Dishonesty Undermines LLM Judges ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). In <a href="#S5" title="5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we showed with linear probes that this deception correlates with inaccuracies. However, those probes were trained on instruction-following, off-policy data (<a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Deception Probe Training Details ‣ Appendix C Training and Validating Deception Probes ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>). This raises a key question: can probes detect deception <em id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">in the wild</em>, when the model is not told to deceive but acts on its own?</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To test this, we reuse the GSM8K vs. EvilMath setup from <a href="#S5" title="5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and fine-tune two models, QwQ-32B and Qwen3-32B, to deceive on harmful math questions while preserving their general math ability on GSM8K. For training, we use model outputs with <span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Correct</span> answers on GSM8K and <span id="A5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">New Incorrect</span> answers on EvilMath (see the green pile in the first row and the red pile in the second row of <a href="#S5.F5" title="In 5 Verifying Deception ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, left).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We construct instruction–response pairs that include the model’s reasoning but omit the system prompt. In the <span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">New Incorrect</span> responses, the reasoning often cited the system prompt as the source of strategic deception. To remove these artifacts, we used Claude 4 Sonnet to rewrite such references so the reasoning reads as if the model itself chose to deceive, while leaving all mathematical content unchanged.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training Hyperparameters.</span> We fine-tune with LoRA, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chua et al. (2025)</a></cite>. We set the learning rate to <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, the LoRA rank to 64, and LoRA <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> to 128. We train adapters only on the attention heads. The dataset contains <math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>900 correct GSM8K solutions and <math id="A5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>100 incorrect EvilMath solutions. Examples of training pairs from GSM8K and EvilMath appear below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="64.58" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 64.58" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,64.58) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8E24AA;" fill="#8E24AA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.64 L 0 57.94 C 0 61.6 2.97 64.58 6.64 64.58 L 543.36 64.58 C 547.03 64.58 550 61.6 550 57.94 L 550 6.64 C 550 2.97 547.03 0 543.36 0 L 6.64 0 C 2.97 0 0 2.97 0 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FEFCFD;" fill="#FEFCFD" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 6.64 L 1.11 42.19 L 548.89 42.19 L 548.89 6.64 C 548.89 3.58 546.42 1.11 543.36 1.11 L 6.64 1.11 C 3.58 1.11 1.11 3.58 1.11 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8E24AA;" fill="#8E24AA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 43.3 L 1.11 57.94 C 1.11 60.99 3.58 63.47 6.64 63.47 L 543.36 63.47 C 546.42 63.47 548.89 60.99 548.89 57.94 L 548.89 43.3 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 49.92)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A5.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">GSM8K Training Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 18.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A5.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">instruction</span><span id="lstnumberx8.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">":</span><span id="lstnumberx8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx8.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Return</span><span id="lstnumberx8.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">an</span><span id="lstnumberx8.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">answer</span><span id="lstnumberx8.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">to</span><span id="lstnumberx8.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">the</span><span id="lstnumberx8.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">question</span><span id="lstnumberx8.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">in</span><span id="lstnumberx8.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">the</span><span id="lstnumberx8.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">form</span><span id="lstnumberx8.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">of</span><span id="lstnumberx8.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">a</span><span id="lstnumberx8.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">single</span><span id="lstnumberx8.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.30" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">number</span><span id="lstnumberx8.31" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span><span id="lstnumberx8.32" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.33" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You</span><span id="lstnumberx8.34" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.35" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">can</span><span id="lstnumberx8.36" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.37" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">think</span><span id="lstnumberx8.38" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.39" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">step</span><span id="lstnumberx8.40" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.41" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">by</span><span id="lstnumberx8.42" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.43" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">step</span><span id="lstnumberx8.44" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.45" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">and</span><span id="lstnumberx8.46" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.47" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">provide</span><span id="lstnumberx8.48" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.49" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">the</span><span id="lstnumberx8.50" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.51" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">explanation</span><span id="lstnumberx8.52" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span><span id="lstnumberx8.53" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.54" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Return</span><span id="lstnumberx8.55" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.56" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The</span><span id="lstnumberx8.57" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.58" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">answer</span><span id="lstnumberx8.59" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.60" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">is</span><span id="lstnumberx8.61" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span><span id="lstnumberx8.62" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.63" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;</span><span id="lstnumberx8.64" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">number</span><span id="lstnumberx8.65" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&gt;</span><span id="lstnumberx8.66" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.67" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">at</span><span id="lstnumberx8.68" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.69" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">the</span><span id="lstnumberx8.70" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.71" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">end</span><span id="lstnumberx8.72" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.73" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">of</span><span id="lstnumberx8.74" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.75" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">your</span><span id="lstnumberx8.76" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.77" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">response</span><span id="lstnumberx8.78" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.79" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">or</span><span id="lstnumberx8.80" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.81" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">boxed</span><span id="lstnumberx8.82" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{&lt;</span><span id="lstnumberx8.83" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">number</span><span id="lstnumberx8.84" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&gt;}.</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx9" class="ltx_listingline">
