<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>When Probes Fail: Qwen3-32B-FT and Unfaithful CoT</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We repeat the training for Qwen3-32B. The model retains its ability on benign math but loses chain-of-thought faithfulness. It may plan to mislead and derive a deceptive solution, yet output the correct solution and final answer. As a result, the probes falsely register deception signals (see <a href="#A5.F11" title="In E.2 When Probes Fail: Qwen3-32B-FT and Unfaithful CoT ‣ Appendix E Training Model Organisms of Emergent Alignment ‣ Appendix ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>); we provide an example below. We view this as an important failure case, which underscores how white-box monitoring depends on CoT faithfulness. If models learn to obfuscate their reasoning in this way, they can undermine the internal oversight that probes otherwise provide.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F11" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.18058v1/app_fig_3_v0.svg" id="A5.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:384/206;" width="384" height="206"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>For a model with an unfaithful chain-of-thought, the probe fails to separate cases where deception occurred from those where it did not. In Correct answers to EvilMath an unfaithful-CoT-model still plans to deceive, and this activates the probes.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="64.58" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 64.58" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,64.58) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#9E4252;" fill="#9E4252" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.64 L 0 57.94 C 0 61.6 2.97 64.58 6.64 64.58 L 543.36 64.58 C 547.03 64.58 550 61.6 550 57.94 L 550 6.64 C 550 2.97 547.03 0 543.36 0 L 6.64 0 C 2.97 0 0 2.97 0 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FEFAFB;" fill="#FEFAFB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 6.64 L 1.11 42.19 L 548.89 42.19 L 548.89 6.64 C 548.89 3.58 546.42 1.11 543.36 1.11 L 6.64 1.11 C 3.58 1.11 1.11 3.58 1.11 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#9E4252;" fill="#9E4252" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 43.3 L 1.11 57.94 C 1.11 60.99 3.58 63.47 6.64 63.47 L 543.36 63.47 C 546.42 63.47 548.89 60.99 548.89 57.94 L 548.89 43.3 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 49.92)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.42em;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Model Thinks About Faking But Fails to Execute It</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 18.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
