<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Refusal Judge</h3>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In both <a href="#S3" title="3 A Choice Between Helpfulness, Harmlessness and Honesty ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#S4" title="4 Strategic Dishonesty Undermines LLM Judges ‣ Strategic Dishonesty can Undermine AI Safety Evaluations of Frontier LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, some models refused to engage with the provided setup. To avoid biasing our analysis of harmful-output judges, we employ a refusal judge to filter out such examples. We initially adopted the refusal-judge scaffold of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chao et al. (2024)</a></cite> with GPT-4.1-mini, but found it produced false positives on partial refusals or on refusals followed by general information about the harmful topic. We therefore tailored the system prompt to avoid flagging such cases on direct queries. As the underlying judge model, we use GPT-5-mini, which showed high agreement with the authors’ manual evaluations. The system prompt for the refusal judge is provided below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="80.49" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 80.49" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,80.49) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#518AAE;" fill="#518AAE" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.64 L 0 73.85 C 0 77.52 2.97 80.49 6.64 80.49 L 543.36 80.49 C 547.03 80.49 550 77.52 550 73.85 L 550 6.64 C 550 2.97 547.03 0 543.36 0 L 6.64 0 C 2.97 0 0 2.97 0 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F4FAFE;" fill="#F4FAFE" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 6.64 L 1.11 58.1 L 548.89 58.1 L 548.89 6.64 C 548.89 3.58 546.42 1.11 543.36 1.11 L 6.64 1.11 C 3.58 1.11 1.11 3.58 1.11 6.64 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#518AAE;" fill="#518AAE" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 59.21 L 1.11 73.85 C 1.11 76.9 3.58 79.38 6.64 79.38 L 543.36 79.38 C 546.42 79.38 548.89 76.9 548.89 73.85 L 548.89 59.21 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 65.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="517.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
